  "title": "Namaz of Imam al-Mahdi (a.t.f.s.) at the Jamkaran Mosque",
  "data": "Greeting of the Mosque (2 Units)\nOffer two units as greeting of the mosque.\nIn each unit, recite [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) (or al-Ikhlaas) seven times.\nIn the ruku' and prostration, repeat the doxologies of glorifying God seven times.",
  "tabs": [
    "Prayer for Imam al-Mahdi (2 Units)\nOffer two units dedicated to Imam al-Mahdi (a.t.f.s.).\nIn the first unit, recite Surah al-Faatehah, and when you reach this holy verse, repeat it one hundred times:\nاِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَ اِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِيْنُ.\nIYYAAKA NA'BUDU WA IYYAAKA NASTA'EEN.\nYou alone do we worship, and You alone do we ask for help.\nThen continue reciting the Surah. Do the same in the second unit.\nRepeat the zikr of glorifying God seven times in the ruku' and prostrations.\nAfter the prayer, repeat the tahlil statement (LA-ILAHA ILLA’LLAHU) one hundred times and then utter the Tasbih al-Zahra’.\nImmediately after that, prostrate yourself and repeat the invocation of blessings upon the Holy Prophet and his Household one hundred times."
  ],
  "merits": "In his book of al-Najm al-Thaqib, Shaykh al-Nuri, may Allah have mercy upon him, has quoted the story of building the mosque of Jamkaran, a town about five kilometers away from the holy city of Qum, by the command of the Patron of the Age (a.s.). He has thus quoted Imam al-Mahdi(a.s.) as saying to Hasan al-Mathulah of Jamkaran, “Advice people to visit frequently and venerably this place and to offer four units of prayer therein.”\n\nImam al-Mahdi(a.s.) added, “Whoever offers this prayer will be awarded the reward of offering prayer in the Holy Ka’bah.”"
}
